From ebf1d67075468a497fb35d458c53738e9c3f4eba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xxavier-ml <Xxavier-ml@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:42:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reorganize the site: one taxonomy, one rhythm, one story per
 page

The site had grown a second structure on top of its first. This puts the
navigation, the marketplace pages and the home page back into one shape.

Navigation (data/navigation.ts, Header, Footer)
- "Browse" and "Explore > All products" both went to /browse, so two labels
  named one page and /browse lit up two nav entries at once. One "Marketplace"
  group now holds Browse, Auctions and Stores.
- The header carried "Sell" and a "Start selling" button to the same page; the
  button is now the app, which is what the site is for.
- The footer filed Roadmap under Product and Vision under Company, and spent a
  whole column on three social links. Header, mobile menu and footer now read
  from the same four groups; social links sit under the brand.
- Desktop menus open on hover and say what each item is.

Home page
- Dropped the "Find / Negotiate / Complete" strip, which restated the four
  capabilities above it in different words. The eight-step version lives on
  /how-it-works, which the capabilities section now links to.
- The hero showed "0 live auctions, 0 online stores" on a quiet day. Live
  counts appear only when there is something to count; the bar is topped up
  with things that are always true.
- The featured grid showed four cards in a three-column grid, leaving an
  orphan card and a hole. Four cards, four columns.
- Section order is now a narrative, and the section list is documented.

Pages and rhythm
- Every section carried 144px top and bottom - 288px of empty space between
  one section's last line and the next section's first. Now 104px, with one
  consistent eyebrow/headline/lead shape.
- Headlines set with hard br tags broke into orphans ("Information doesn't /
  flow / where it's needed."). The breaks are gone and text-wrap: balance
  does the work.
- The catalogue hero was 585px of marketing above the products; it is now a
  header. Category chips ran 2924px inside a 1240px box, hiding 13 of 21
  categories behind a "swipe" hint on desktop; they wrap on wide screens.
- Status tabs, search and categories are one filter panel instead of three
  controls floating on the starfield.
- Empty auction and store lists offered nothing to do next; they now link to
  the catalogue, the other marketplace and the app.
- tsconfig.tsbuildinfo is ignored.
